    "output": "1. This screen wants me to read which loan costs less and then finish, since it says I can stop here.\n\n2. \"I'm done\"\n\n3. Words that felt like tech talk or were unclear:\n- \"Interest and fees\". I sort of know interest, but the two together are fuzzy.\n- \"Costs less to borrow\". It's not clear whether that means the total or the monthly payment.\n- \"Estimate\". I'm not sure how rough it is.\n- \"More options\". I don't know what options, and it's not clear how it differs from \"Change my numbers\".\n- \"See all the numbers\". Which numbers, and aren't those already above?\n- \"Step 5 of 5\". Fine, but I wondered if that meant I could not go back.\n- The two lines \"$1,437.91 $373.27 a month\" sit side by side with no label. I had to guess that the first is the total and the second is the monthly payment.\n- \"Print or save\". I don't know where it saves.\n\n4. Worries:\n- The screen says Offer 1 costs less, but Offer 2 has the smaller monthly payment. Being told two different things made me unsure which to pick, and I worried about choosing the wrong loan.\n- \"I'm done\" could mean it submits or applies for something. It doesn't say nothing is sent.\n- \"Print or save\" made me wonder whether my numbers are being stored somewhere.\n- The last line says the lender statement has the final numbers. That made me unsure how far to trust this screen.\n- I don't know whether \"Change my numbers\" erases what I already typed.\n\n5. What I would skip:\n- \"More options\"\n- \"See all the numbers\"\n- \"What the words mean\". I would only open it if I got stuck, and I didn't know it would help with the words that confused me.\n\n6. Score: 3. I know the button to tap, but I'm unsure which loan I should choose.\n\nRESULT: {\"next_tap\":\"I'm done\",\"confusing_terms\":[\"interest and fees\",\"costs less to borrow\",\"estimate\",\"More options\",\"See all the numbers\",\"unlabeled total and monthly figures\",\"Print or save\"],\"worries\":[\"Offer 1 is ch